3 | STAFFING A STATISTICAL COLLABORATION UNIT
Just as the infrastructure and budget support may differ among statistical collaboration units, staffing models may vary among centres. Statistical
collaboration unit staff actively contribute to a diverse set of research projects (prospective, retrospective, small and large datasets, experimental
and observational studies, etc.), from study design all the way through dissemination. This diversity provides a wide array of opportunities for
applying different statistical and data-driven methodologies, as well as addressing a variety of research questions. The diversity in research
