While the field of data science and (bio)statistical consulting and collaboration is always changing, it is a vibrant and exciting field in which to
build a programme or a career. Statistical collaboration and consulting units play a crucial role in creating and enabling high quality, rigorous and
reproducible research and innovation across the globe. Their connections to students make them vital in training and preparing the next genera
tion of collaborative statisticians and data scientists to solve complex problems through data centric decision-making. Careful planning and imple
mentation that addresses this manuscript's three themes of infrastructure and fiscal budget, staffing and professional development lay the
foundation to guide these essential units to successful futures.
